  "mappingSource": "WinWing 3M.PDC 1 manual section 3.2 \"Buttons\" drawing (page 12/29, https://eu.winctrl.com/static/ipfs/QmRZUBzvsURGGZ84ma9T4LRS5gEVekPFf3qjWmJeNmb82g), checked: matches the catalog (1 FPV, 2 MTRS, 3 VSD, 4-10 WXR..TERR, 11/12/13 VOR 1/OFF/ADF 1, 14/15/16 VOR 2/OFF/ADF 2, 17 RST, 18 CTR, 19 TFC, 20 STD, 21/22 RANGE -/+, 25/26 RADIO/BARO, 27/28 IN/HPA, 29-32 APP/VOR/MAP/PLN, MINS spring knob 33/34/35/36/37, BARO spring knob 23/38/39/40/24); catalog also cites the X-Plane plugin Zibo PDC table (https://github.com/rswilem/winctrl-xplane-plugin)",
  "confidence": "high",
  "note": "The catalog note says \"not cross-checked against the 3M manual drawing\": it is now, and it matches. MINS and BARO are stacked knobs: black push cap (RST / STD), front cream spring knob (slow 34/36 or 38/40 = rotary part; far positions 33/37 or 23/24 and centre 35 or 39 = button parts, all on that same knob), rear larger cream ring = RADIO/BARO or IN/HPA selector. The spring-knob position parts sit around the front knob (medium: one physical knob, several parts). VSD is partly hidden behind the BARO knob.",
